  "id": "secondary-coping",
  "term": "secondary coping",
  "definition": "Secondary coping is a way of responding to stress by changing oneself or the way one interprets the situation, rather than trying to change the outside circumstances directly. It is contrasted with primary coping, which focuses on altering the external environment through action.",
